        "original_id": "8fd0070c-bf0b-5bae-9419-122feb7f6a94",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leigh Silverman, Jeanine Tesori, Brian Crawley, Doris Betts\n- Works: Violet, From Up Here, Chinglish, The Ugliest Pilgrim\n- Roles: stage director, composer, librettist\n- Awards: Tony Award, Drama Desk Award\n\nFacts:\n- Leigh Silverman is an American stage director who has worked both Off-Broadway and on Broadway.\n- In 2008, Leigh Silverman was nominated for the Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Director of a Play for From Up Here.\n- In 2011, Chinglish opened on Broadway with direction by Leigh Silverman.\n- Chinglish is a comedy about an American businessman who is desperate to launch a new enterprise in China.\n- In 2014, Leigh Silverman was nominated for the Tony Award for Best Direction of a Musical for Violet.\n- Violet is a musical with music by Jeanine Tesori and a libretto by Brian Crawley.\n- Violet is based on the short story The Ugliest Pilgrim by Doris Betts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
